extends shared/layout.pug

block content

  h2 Create a feed
  
  p Here you can create a feed for your chatroom or any RSS feed reader
  
  div(class='accordion' id='feedsetup')
    div(class='card')
      div(class='card-header' id='create')
        h3(class='mb-0')
          button(class='btn btn-primary' data-toggle='collapse' data-target='#createCnt' aria-expanded='true' aria-controls='createCnt') Understand the path
      div(id='createCnt' class='collapse show' aria-labelledby='create' data-parent='#feedsetup')
        div(class='card-body')
          p you'll be creating an RSS feed url that start with 
            code https://sefeeds.socvr.org
            | followed by the path 
            code /hnq/ 
            | and ends with 
            | the selection of the site or sites. Start with an so called operation character, followed by (part of) the url of the site for the operation
            | there are three operators that can be prepended to the url to search for:
          ul
            li +  To include the sites that match
            li -  To exclude the sites that match
            li =  To achieve an exact match
    div(class='card')
      div(class='card-header' id='combine')
        h3(class='mb-0')
          button(class='btn btn-primary' data-toggle='collapse' data-target='#combineCnt' aria-expanded='false' aria-controls='combineCnt') Make the selection
      div(id='combineCnt' class='collapse' aria-labelledby='combine' data-parent='#feedsetup')
        div(class='card-body')
          p You can combine multiple operators from one feed, remember you don't need the whole server name. 
          p For example a feed for Super User and Server Fault you would use 
            code +superuser+serverfault
          p A feed for all sites that end with cs but not electronics the url would end in 
            code +cs-electronics
          p A feed for an exact match on mathoverflow.net you would use 
            code =mathoverflow.net
          p Or use a filter 
            code +?filter=(display_score gt 50) or (answer_count gt 10)
          p Tip: You can test your feed by pasting the whole url in the addressbar of your browser. See the examples below in Ready made Feeds
    div(class='card')
      div(class='card-header' id='advFilt')
        h3(class='mb-0')
          button(class='btn btn-primary' data-toggle='collapse' data-target='#advFiltCnt' aria-expanded='false' aria-controls='advFiltCnt') Advanced filter
      div(id='advFiltCnt' class='collapse' aria-labelledby='install' data-parent='#feedsetup')
        div(class='card-body')
          p For creating a feed that is not based on sites but on other criteria you can create your own filter. A filter gets applied after the site selection. You can use a single + to inlude all sites.
          p A filter is added as a query parameter named filter and is followed by an expression. In the expression values and fields can be compared with several operators and/or functions
          p This are the operators / functions / logic
          ol 
            li eq Equals
            li ne not equals
            li gt Greater than
            li gte Greater than or equals
            li lt Less  than
            li lte Less than or equals
            li not negate
            li contains 
            li and both expressions need to true
            li or  one of the expressions is true
          p Use paranthesis to group expressions. For example <code>(display_score gt 50) and (answer_count lt 3)</code>. String values go between single quotes <code>tags contains 'number'</code>
          p The following fields are available: site; tags; display_score; answer_count; title; user_name; question_id; icon_url; creation_date
          p Try the url in the address bar of your browser first and copy the url once you have result. This is to prevent 
            a(href='https://meta.stackexchange.com/q/352848/158100') encoding problems
            
    div(class='card')
      div(class='card-header' id='install')
        h3(class='mb-0')
          button(class='btn btn-primary' data-toggle='collapse' data-target='#installCnt' aria-expanded='false' aria-controls='installCnt') Setup the feed
      div(id='installCnt' class='collapse' aria-labelledby='install' data-parent='#feedsetup')
        div(class='card-body')
          p If you have included/excluded all you need and created the complete RSS feed url you setup your chatroom:
          ol
           li Goto the info page of your chatroom
           li Click on the Feeds tab
           li Scroll to the Add a new feed section 
           li Clickin the textbox after 
             i New feed items from the URL
           li Paste your url in the textbox
           li Select how you want to feed items to appear 
           li Click 
             i add this feed
          p Refer to this 
           a(href='/images/add-feed.PNG') screenshot 
           | in case something is unclear
          p You're all set now.

  p
  
  h3 Ready made feeds

  p Here are some read-to-go examples for Hot Network Questions from around the Stack Exchange Network, including Stack Overflow

  div(class='row')
    div(class='col-sm-4')
      div(class='card')
        div(class='card-body')
          h5(class='card-title') Ask Ubuntu
          p(class='card-text')
            pre /hnq/askubuntu
          a(class='btn btn-primary btn-info' href='https://sefeeds.socvr.org/hnq/askubuntu' target='_blank')
           | Try it here
    div(class='col-sm-4')
      div(class='card')
        div(class='card-body')
          h5(class='card-title') The English sites
          p(class='card-text')
            pre /hnq/ell+english
          a(class='btn btn-primary btn-info' href='https://sefeeds.socvr.org/hnq/ell+english' target='_blank')
           | Try it here
    div(class='col-sm-4')
      div(class='card')
        div(class='card-body')
          h5(class='card-title') Not Stack Exchange
          p(class='card-text')
            pre /hnq/-stackexchange
          a(class='btn btn-primary btn-info' href='https://sefeeds.socvr.org/hnq/-stackexchange' target='_blank')
           | Try it here
  div(class='row mt-4')
    div(class='col-sm-4')
      div(class='card')
        div(class='card-body')
          h5(class='card-title') Trilogy
          p(class='card-text')
            pre /hnq/stacko+super+fault
          a(class='btn btn-primary btn-info' href='https://sefeeds.socvr.org/hnq/stackoverflow+super+serverfault' target='_blank')
           | Try it here
    div(class='col-sm-4')
      div(class='card')
        div(class='card-body')
          h5(class='card-title') Exact match
          p(class='card-text')
            pre /hnq/=cs.stackexchange.com
          a(class='btn btn-primary btn-info' href='https://sefeeds.socvr.org/hnq/=cs.stackexchange.com' target='_blank')
           | Try it here
  div(class='row mt-4')
    div(class='col-sm-8')
      div(class='card')
        div(class='card-body')
          h5(class='card-title') Advanced Filter
          p(class='card-text')
            pre /hnq/+?filter=(display_score gt 50) or (answer_count gt 10)
          a(class='btn btn-primary btn-info' href='https://sefeeds.socvr.org/hnq/+?filter=(display_score gt 50) or (answer_count gt 10)' target='_blank')
           | Try it here

